menuconfig HMI
    bool "HMI library"
    imply LVGL
    select LV_USE_ARC
    select LV_USE_LABEL
    select LV_USE_BUTTON
    select LV_USE_FLEX
    select LV_USE_SLIDER
    select LV_USE_BAR
    select LV_USE_TABVIEW
    select LV_USE_CHART
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_12
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_16
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_18
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_22
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_28
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_32
    select LV_FONT_MONTSERRAT_38
    help
      Gauge-style HMI widgets and app lifecycle (hmi_init/hmi_show)
      built on the LVGL module. Consumers just set CONFIG_HMI=y and
      #include <hmi/hmi.h>.

      Requires the LVGL module to be present in the workspace; the
      required LVGL widgets and fonts are selected here. Display
      specific settings (color depth, memory pool, VDB size) and the
      zephyr,display chosen node remain the consumer's responsibility.

